to investigate design and development controls (ISO 13485 Clause 7.3) regarding software automation for class II/III devices."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-art83-pms-system", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Supports the obligation to actively gather, record, and analyze relevant data on device safety throughout its lifetime per EU MDR Article 83."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The incident involves a discordance between bedside monitor logs and cloud-side classifier logs regarding the detection of complete atrioventricular block (AVB). Although no adverse patient outcome was recorded in this specific instance, the disagreement on whether the threshold was met indicates a potential failure or missed detection in a safety-critical function. Under FDA QMSR 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c), manufacturers must comply with design and development controls (ISO 13485 Clause 7.3) which includes validation of software algorithms used for device automation. The existence of conflicting logs suggests the algorithm's performance in real-world conditions may not match expectations or that data integrity/traceability issues exist, requiring investigation under post-market surveillance obligations per EU MDR Article 83(1)-(2). While contained (no harm realized), the potential for serious harm if this discordance were to occur with a patient-dependent decision is significant enough to warrant Severity 3. The lack of direct technical evidence linking the specific code change or configuration causing the log disagreement in the retrieved artifacts lowers confidence and necessitates human review.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "9c3078386d220fc93912c5ace023d58e7a2d7842ab4bf8f305b41f4143e5f581", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id"